Circle Step 51: RP1 (Raspberry Pi 5) I2C master fixes for mt32-pi

- Recover the bus (TODO in Circle): if SDA is stuck low after a failed
  transfer, or before a new one, clock SCL by hand until the slave releases
  it, then send START and STOP. Also done when the bus stays busy.
- Reads that fail with "arbitration lost" after all but the last byte have
  arrived return the bytes received. The MiSTer mt32pi I2C slave drives ACK
  after every byte, including the last byte of a read, which collides with
  the master's NACK; the DesignWare controller then aborts, drops that byte
  and leaves the slave holding SDA low. (The Pi 3/4 BSC ignores this.)
  Callers can read one byte more than they need.
- Optionally wait for events (WFE) instead of polling at full speed while a
  transfer is in progress (g_bI2CMasterIdleWait). Only for applications that
  enable the generic timer event stream on every core that uses I2C.
- Record the last abort source/error, recovery and partial read counts in
  globals for application diagnostics.

